      "message": "I think handling it here is fine -- this is the kind of thing that only happens with fuzzer-crafted inputs. Doing it `onCombineIfPossible` is going to be trickier, because we\u0027d need to call `computeRegionComplexity`. However, I\u0027d suggest using `SkSafeMath` (we do similar things elsewhere). You can make an `SkSafeMath` object on the stack, use it to do all the integer addition, and then just check the safe-math object (it converts to bool) at the end. I\u0027d also skip the assert (otherwise fuzzers are going to generate bugs when they can generate the resulting crash.",
